{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"bbcb7bb9-e211-4633-b082-15da7a22bac7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"An in-memory sliding window rate limiter with burst allowance, concurrent thread safety, comprehensive type annotations, and full unit test coverage is implemented in [`src/rate_limiter.py`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/rate_limiter.py) and [`src/test_rate_limiter.py`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py).\n\n---\n\n### Implementation Overview\n\n#### 1. Rate Limiter Core ([`src/rate_limiter.py`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/rate_limiter.py))\n- **Sliding Window Algorithm**: Tracks request timestamps and costs per key using double-ended queues (`collections.deque`), expiring out-of-window requests on each access with an $O(k)$ cleanup where $k$ is the number of expired entries.\n- **Burst Allowance**: Sustained rate limit is extended by `burst_allowance`, allowing up to `max_capacity = limit + burst_allowance` requests within any rolling `window_seconds`.\n- **Concurrency \u0026 Thread Safety**: Uses `threading.Lock()` across all state inspections and mutations to guarantee atomic admission checks and prevent race conditions.\n- **Key Partitioning**: Independent buckets per key (e.g., user ID, API token, IP address) with fallback to `\"default\"`.\n- **Dynamic Costs**: Supports weighted request costs with input validation.\n- **Type Annotations**: Comprehensive annotations across all functions, parameters, and attributes (`Deque[Tuple[float, int]]`, `Dict[str, Deque[...]]`, `Optional[float]`, etc.).\n\n#### 2. Unit Tests ([`src/test_rate_limiter.py`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py))\n- [`test_initialization_validation`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L15-L33): Verifies input validation on non-positive limits/windows and negative burst allowances.\n- [`test_basic_rate_limiting`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L34-L41): Verifies strictly enforcing limit quotas.\n- [`test_burst_allowance`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L42-L53): Verifies burst allowance capacity (`limit + burst_allowance`).\n- [`test_sliding_window_expiration`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L54-L69): Tests continuous time-based roll-off of requests past `window_seconds`.\n- [`test_custom_cost`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L70-L85): Validates multi-unit costs and rejection when remaining quota is insufficient.\n- [`test_key_isolation`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L86-L95): Tests partition isolation across distinct keys.\n- [`test_reset`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L96-L113): Tests selective and global quota resets.\n- [`test_concurrent_thread_safety`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_rate_limiter.py#L114-L147): Spawns 20 threads contending across a synchronized barrier with 200 total requests, asserting exact capacity admission without over-allocation.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n\nAll 8 unit tests execute and pass:\n```bash\npython -m unittest src/test_rate_limiter.py\n........\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 8 tests in 0.004s\n\nOK\n```\n","duration_seconds":17.5162263,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":73507,"output_tokens":1468,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":138876,"total_tokens":74975}}}
